 "title": "Treasurer | Muskegon County, MI",
 "text": "Treasurer | Muskegon County, MI\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nSearch\nCounty Government\nCourts\nVisit Muskegon\nHow Do I...\nHome\nCounty Government\nDepartments K-Z\nTreasurer\nTreasurer\nOffice Open to the Public 8 AM to 4:45 PM Monday - Friday\nA Dropbox has been installed on the side of the building to accept payments. To pay by credit, visit www.GovPayNow.com or\ncall 1-888-604-7888. (Pay Location Code #6896)\nResponsibilities\nThe primary goal of the office is to collect delinquent property taxes for the County of Muskegon. Through this office, the money is then invested in various forms to make additional operating capital for the County.\nPayments\nThe Treasurer's Office does accept partial payments on delinquent taxes in most situations. The deadline for redeeming delinquent taxes is two years. Property is sold at public auction approximately two and a half years after it becomes delinquent. For more information regarding this procedure, please stop by the office for a copy of the tax sale guidelines.\nTax Records\nThe Treasurer's Office is also responsible for keeping permanent records of tax rolls, delinquent tax rolls, tax histories for various public agencies, banks, mortgage title companies and other interested parties at a nominal cost.\nDeposits & Fees\nOther functions include receiving County department deposits and making those deposits to various banks. They also collect probation payments, incarceration fees and certify that all taxes are current for recording of deeds. Dog licenses can also be purchased at the Treasurer's office.\nQuick Links\nPay Delinquent Property Tax Online\nDLQ ACH Form\nDog License Application (PDF)\nForeclosed Property Auction\n5743 Notice of Intention to Claim Interest\nView All Links\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nContact Us\nTony Moulatsiotis\nTreasurer\nPhone: 231-724-6261\nTreasurer\nEmail Treasurer\nPhysical Address\nView Map\n1903 Marquette Ave\nSuite A103\nMuskegon , MI 49442\n1903 Marquette Ave Suite A103 Muskegon MI 49442\nDirections\nPhone: 231-724-6261\nFax: 231-724-6549\nDirectory\nContact Us\nContracts\nCounty Settlement Data\n2025 Settlement Data\n2024 Settlement Data\n2023 Settlement Data\n2022 Settlement Data\n2021 Settlement Data\n2020 Settlement Data\n2019 Settlement Data\n2018 Settlement Data\n2017 Settlement Data\n2016 Settlement Data\n2015 Settlement Data\n2014 Settlement Data\n2013 Settlement Data\n2012 Settlement Data\n2011 Settlement Data\n2010 Settlement Data\n2009 Settlement Data\n2008 Settlement Data\n2007 Settlement Data\n2006 Settlement Data\n2005 Settlement Data\nDog Licenses\nHow Do I Apply for a New License?\nHow Much Does a Dog Licenses Cost?\nWhat Else Should Dog Owners Know?\nWhere Can I Apply for / Renew My Dog's License?\nForms\nMillage Rates (PDF)\nProperty Taxes\nAvoiding Foreclosure\nDeadlines for Property Taxes\nFAQs\nFinancial Hardship Policy & Application\nPay Delinquent Property Tax Online\nProperty Tax Search\nTop 12 Taxpayers Per School District\nBoard of Commissioners Meetings Schedule View agendas and watch live.\nEmployment Opportunities View current job listings with Muskegon County.\nFOIA- Freedom of Information Act Requests for public records.\n-->\nContact Us\nTreasurer\nEmail Treasurer\nPhysical Address\n1903 Marquette Ave\nSuite A103\nMuskegon , MI 49442\nPhone: 231-724-6261\nFax: 231-724-6549\nDirectory\nSite Links\nHome\nSite Map\nContact Us\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\nPrivacy Policy\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by CivicPlus®\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nClose ×",
